```c
const u8 curve25519_null_point[CURVE25519_KEY_SIZE] __aligned(32) = { 0 };
const u8 curve25519_base_point[CURVE25519_KEY_SIZE] __aligned(32) = { 9 };
EXPORT_SYMBOL(curve25519_null_point);
EXPORT_SYMBOL(curve25519_base_point);
EXPORT_SYMBOL(curve25519_generic);
```

Code statements:
```c
const u8 curve25519_null_point[CURVE25519_KEY_SIZE] __aligned(32) = { 0 };
const u8 curve25519_base_point[CURVE25519_KEY_SIZE] __aligned(32) = { 9 };
EXPORT_SYMBOL(curve25519_null_point);
EXPORT_SYMBOL(curve25519_base_point);
EXPORT_SYMBOL(curve25519_generic);
```

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (CRYPTO_CURVE25519 == y) 
    CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519_GENERIC = y;
if (CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519 == m) 
    // architecture-specific functions not available
```
Reason:
The self-test code for Curve25519 was incorrectly controlled by the GENERIC configuration option, which could be enabled while the architecture-specific library (CRYPTO_LIB_CURVE25519) was set to a module (m). This resulted in undefined references to architecture-specific functions during the build process, as those functions were not available when the self-test code was compiled.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
// Split GENERIC module from CURVE25519 module
EXPORT_SYMBOL(curve25519_generic);
```
Reason:
The patch separates the GENERIC module from the CURVE25519 module, ensuring that the self-test code is only enabled when the overall CURVE25519 option is selected. This prevents the self-test from being compiled when the architecture-specific functions are not available, thus resolving the undefined reference errors during the build process.

